  "description": "LUYBOX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C94 H119 Eu3 N6 O16 S8,C96 H125 Eu3 N5 O14 S9,3(C3 H7 N1 O1),4(C2 H3 N1),4.25(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu5 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu6 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.580-4.764 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.14-166.50°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C94H119Eu3N6O16S8·C96H125Eu3N5O14S9·3(dmf)·4(MeCN)·4.25(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
